    "checks": [
      "The unit must be inside the main building. A detached garage 'shall not include a dwelling' (19-501.l(5))",
      "Only one building for residential use per lot in R-1, R-2, R-3H, R-OA and UV (19-501.l(1))",
      "Family means persons 'related by blood (within and including the degree of first cousin), marriage or adoption' (19-201). Others count as unrelated",
      "A student home may be in a one-family dwelling with an apartment. In R-1, R-2 and R-3 student homes have spacing, floor area, parking and permit rules (19-501.l(6))",
      "Renting any dwelling unit needs a housing permit from the Code Official. In State College the threshold is 1 day (4-504b(3), amending Centre Region code 802.1)",
      "Short-term rental: allowed with a license in all zones. The apartment may be rented short term only if the owner or tenant lives in the main dwelling. Limit 120 days a year (10-901b, 10-906a and c)",
      "District permission for R-2 to UV comes through 'Any use permitted in' chains back to R-1. Confirm with the Planning Department",
      "Parking is the one open reading: 2 or 4 spaces in total. Ask the Zoning Officer"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Borough Planning Department. Rewrite page: https://www.statecollegepa.us/225/New-Zoning-Ordinance. Pending: a new comprehensive Zoning Ordinance and SALDO are in draft. A revised draft was posted for public review as of June 1, 2026, and Council meetings ran through Sep 9, 2026. A news report says Council may add ADU rules. Not adopted. Not law."
  },
